  "title": "Australians Opt Out of Social Media Algorithms",
  "summary": "Australians are set to opt out of social media algorithms, with the government planning to force users to easily switch in or out of personalized content. The legislation aims to boost online safety and limit exposure to harmful content.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Australians are set to opt out of social media algorithms, with the government planning to force users to easily switch in or out of personalized content.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The proposed legislation aims to boost online safety and limit exposure to harmful content.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Users over 16 years of age will be given new tools to turn off algorithm-driven content, with platforms facing fines of more than A$100m for non-compliance.",
